* /**
*  * @file GIT.REPO
*  * @version 1.0
*  */
* GIT.REPO(repo) — the repository this account belongs to, found the way git
* finds it: start here and walk up the parent directories until a `.git` turns
* up.
*
* The verb used to assume the repository was `.git` inside the account, which is
* only true when the account IS the repository root.  An account can sit below
* one — a repo holding several accounts, or an account inside a larger project —
* and then the assumption is wrong in the worst way: GIT INIT creates a SECOND
* repository nested in the first and splits the history in two, silently.
*
* The test for "is there a repository here" is `<dir>/.git/HEAD`, a plain file
* every repository has, read through GIT.OSFILE so it works on both platforms.
* Testing for the directory itself would need a stat the BASIC has no portable
* spelling for; the HEAD file is equally conclusive and readable anywhere.
*
* Finding NOTHING is not a failure: it means this account is not inside a repo
* yet, and `.git` here is exactly what GIT INIT should create.  So the fallback
* is the account's own path, which is what every caller assumed before.
      SUBROUTINE GIT.REPO(REPO)
      $INCLUDE BP.INC PLATFORM.H
*     WHERE THE ACCOUNT IS, ON A PLATFORM THAT MAY NOT HAVE @PATH.
*
*     @PATH names the account on the session platforms.  MVX has no such system
*     variable — the compiler does not define it, so reading it yields an
*     unassigned variable and a runtime warning — and it does not need one: the
*     account IS the working directory there, which is why every MVX handler
*     passes ".git" as a literal.
*
*     So the reference is guarded rather than merely defaulted.  Without any of
*     this the walk below started at "" and the fallback produced "/.git" — an
*     absolute path at the root of the filesystem, resolving nowhere — which is
*     what a handler written for all three platforms got when it asked.
      ACCT = "."
      $IFNDEF MVX
      ACCT = @PATH
      IF ACCT = "" THEN ACCT = "."
      $ENDIF
      DIR = ACCT
      REPO = ""
*     Both of GIT.OSFILE's outputs start assigned: on MVX neither of its platform
*     arms is compiled in, so it leaves DATA untouched and the runtime warns
*     about an unassigned variable on every step of the walk.
      HEADC = "" ; HOK = 0
      LOOP
         CALL GIT.OSFILE("READ", DIR : "/.git/HEAD", HEADC, HOK)
         IF HOK THEN
            REPO = DIR : "/.git"
            RETURN
         END
*        Step up one directory.  Stop at the root: "/" has no parent, and a
*        relative path that runs out of separators has nowhere left to go.
         SL = 0
         FOR K = LEN(DIR) TO 2 STEP -1
            IF DIR[K, 1] = "/" THEN
               SL = K
               K = 1                      ;* found the last separator — stop
            END
         NEXT K
         IF SL < 2 THEN EXIT
         DIR = DIR[1, SL - 1]
      REPEAT
*     No repository above us: this account is not in one yet.
      REPO = ACCT : "/.git"
      RETURN
      END

